{% doc %}
  A customer replying to a closed ticket reopens it, to the status flagged
  is_reopen_target, and the move is logged.

  @param {object} ticket - The closed ticket
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  function target = 'modules/support/queries/statuses/flagged', flag: 'is_reopen_target'
  if target == blank
    log 'ERROR: no reopen target status in modules/support/commands/tickets/reopen'
    return nil
  endif

  function previous = 'modules/support/queries/statuses/find', id: ticket.status_id

  comment
    Through the same helper every other status change uses, so that a
    reopened ticket forgets both stamps rather than one. Naming only
    closed_at here left solved_at alone, which meant a ticket that went
    Confirmation, Closed, then reopened by a customer still claimed to
    have been solved at a time it was now very much not.
  endcomment
  function stamps = 'modules/support/helpers/status/stamps', status: target
  graphql updated = 'modules/support/tickets/set_status', id: ticket.id, status_id: target.id, closed_at: stamps.closed_at, solved_at: stamps.solved_at

  assign activity = { "ticket_id": ticket.id, "actor_id": null, "action": "reopened", "from_value": previous.name, "to_value": target.name }
  function _ = 'modules/support/commands/activities/create', object: activity

  return updated.record
%}
